  lblTerms:'Unified glossary (one term per line)', lblTermsShort:'Unified glossary', termsPh:'One per line: source → rendering; a line with only the source term keeps the original',
  lblMaxW:'Single-language width in full-width UNITS, not characters: 1 CJK char = 1; Latin, Cyrillic, Thai and Arabic letters = 0.5, so 1 unit is about 2 characters for half-width scripts. Governs monolingual wrapping and "- A - B" dual-speaker lines in bilingual export. Default follows the Netflix spec per language (zh/ko 16, ja 13, others 21). Larger = longer lines, fewer line breaks and cue splits.', lblBiMaxW:'Max width of the TRANSLATED line in bilingual export (same full-width unit, not characters: the same 32 is about 32 Chinese characters but about 64 Thai characters). Constrains the translated line only; the source line follows semantic breaks and is not width-limited, and dual-speaker lines use "Single-language width" above. Exceeding it is the only thing that splits the timeline. This value does NOT change per language. Larger = fewer splits but longer translated lines.', btnGo:'▶ Start translation', btnGoStop:'Translating… click to stop', lyricTip:'How to handle lyric lines: translate / keep the original text / remove them entirely. Lines are matched by the characters in “Lyric markers”.', marksTip:'Subtitle lines containing any of these characters are treated as lyrics. Default ♪♫♬♩ — add or remove freely; leave empty to restore the default. If your file uses no music symbols, add the marker it does use. When a line mixes lyrics with dialogue, “Remove” falls back to keeping the original so dialogue is never deleted.', lyricSkipKeep:'{0} lyric group(s) kept in the original language (not translated)', lyricSkipDrop:'{0} lyric group(s) removed per your setting', lyricWarn:'Heads up: {0}% of lines were classified as lyrics — the marker set may be too broad. Please check and re-run.', dropFillersTip:'On: lines that the local rule judges to be pure filler (um, uh, meaningless humming) are removed outright and never sent to the model, so the result is deterministic. Off: every line goes to the model, which decides case by case whether to translate, keep or drop it. On by default.',
