  tcCvN:'Format Converter',tcCvD:'Convert between 7 formats: SRT / VTT / ASS and more',tcBiN:'Bilingual Splitter',tcBiD:'Split bilingual subtitles into source and translation tracks',tcShN:'Timeline Shift',tcShD:'Global offset, rescale, merge, split, cue-by-cue tweak',tcRpN:'Garbled Text Fix',tcRpD:'Detect the misread encoding and undo the garble',tcExN:'Text Extractor',tcExD:'Pull plain dialogue out of subtitles, two layouts',
  detCvT:'Convert subtitle formats in one step',detCvL:'SRT, VTT, ASS, SBV, LRC—if the file will not load in your player, just convert it. Timings and text are kept character for character, and same-timeline bilingual pairs never stack into two lines.',detCv1:'Reads SRT / VTT / ASS / SSA / SBV / LRC / TXT — 7 formats',detCv2:'Exports SRT / VTT / ASS / SBV / LRC / TXT — 6 formats',detCv3:'Timings and text preserved verbatim; nothing re-ordered or dropped',detCv4:'Four bilingual modes: keep / source only / translation only / smart dedupe',detCvCta:'Open Format Converter',
  detBiT:'Split bilingual subtitles into two clean tracks',detBiL:'Source and translation crammed into one cue, or a bilingual ASS that converts into two stacked lines—four modes take it apart: keep both, source only, translation only, or split into two files with their own timelines.',detBi1:'Two lines in one cue: the source line is told by writing system',detBi2:'Two cues on the same timeline: tracks are separated by order of appearance',detBi3:'Never assumes the translation is Chinese—English-Japanese, English-French all work',detBi4:'Text only is touched; the timeline stays untouched',detBiCta:'Open Bilingual Splitter',
  detShT:'Timings off? Just shift them',detShL:'Subtitles half a second early or late, frame-rate mismatch, merging and splitting, cue-by-cue fine-tuning—all in one page. The output keeps the original format, file header and all.',detSh1:'Global offset: accepts +1.5s, -500ms, or plain milliseconds',detSh2:'Rescale: fix 23.976 vs 25 frame-rate drift in one click',detSh3:'Merge / split: join neighboring cues freely; long lines split on word boundaries',detSh4:'Timeline checkup: four rulers scan the file, flagging suggestions without touching anything',detShCta:'Open Timeline Shift',
  detRpT:'Garbled subtitles, restored to what they really are',detRpL:'Opened the file and got gibberish like "æ—¥æœ¬èªž"? The encoding was most likely misread. Detect whether it was GBK or Shift_JIS, undo the misreading, and save it in the encoding you want.',detRp1:'Recognizes UTF-8 / GBK / Big5 / Shift_JIS / EUC-KR / Latin-1',detRp2:'Pasted text works too; if too much is lost, it says so honestly',detRp3:'The file is usually fine—the result card is always there, saving UTF-8 by default',detRp4:'Save as six encodings; a detected mismatch defaults to BOM',detRpCta:'Open Garbled Text Fix',
  detExT:'Pull the dialogue out of your subtitles',detExL:'For notes, articles, or feeding a model, you want plain text, not timecodes. Continuous paragraphs read like an article; one line per cue reads like a list. Hearing-impaired captions, watermarks and repeated lines are dropped along the way.',detEx1:'Reads SRT / VTT / ASS / SBV / LRC / TXT',detEx2:'Two layouts: paragraphs by pause and punctuation, or one line per cue',detEx3:'Optionally remove SDH captions, watermark lines, and adjacent duplicates',detEx4:'Speaker prefixes and lyric lines are kept by default, one click to drop',detExCta:'Open Text Extractor',
  mkN5:'Commas become dots, cue numbers fade—content untouched',mkN6:'Two independent files, timelines carried over intact',mkN7:'Global 0.5s shift: every cue moves together, gaps unchanged',mkN8:'Detect the original encoding and undo the misreading',mkN9:'Timecodes fade away; only the dialogue remains',mkWas:'Before',mkNow:'After',mkGarbled:'Garbled',mkFixed:'Fixed',tcGlN:'Term Replace',tcGlD:'One glossary rewrites the whole file',detGlT:'One wording, right through the whole file',detGlL:'Character names drifting between episodes, proper nouns spelled three ways, odd words left behind by machine translation — write a glossary and let it run. Timing, ASS styles and VTT note blocks stay byte-identical.',detGl1:'One rule per line: old term -> new term; # starts a comment',detGl2:'Whole-word matching, case sensitivity, bilingual cues can be limited to one line',detGl3:'Works with SRT / VTT / ASS / SBV / LRC / TXT',detGl4:'Every change is listed; any line you regret goes back with one click',detGlCta:'Open term replace',mkN10:'Change the glossary, the whole file follows',/* v0.9.70 两段式界面新增 */
  tcVsN:'Video Subtitle Rip',
  tcVsD:'Pull the embedded subtitle track out of MKV / MP4',
  detVsT:'The subtitle track sealed inside your video, pulled straight out',
  detVsL:'MKV and MP4 files often carry a finished subtitle track — your player can show it, but you cannot get at the text. Rip the whole track out to SRT / VTT / ASS / TXT. Nothing is uploaded and nothing is re-encoded: the file is read inside your own browser.',
  detVs1:'Reads SRT, ASS and WebVTT tracks in MKV / WebM, plus mov_text / tx3g in MP4',
  detVs2:'ASS tracks come back with the original style header and resolution, not a regenerated one',
  detVs3:'Reads in small slices by file offset, so a multi-gigabyte movie never fills up memory',
  detVs4:'Image-based subtitles (DVD / Blu-ray PGS) have no text to rip, and it says so plainly — those need OCR',
  detVsCta:'Open video subtitle rip',
