  tcTbN:'Subtitles ⇄ Spreadsheet',
  tcTbD:'Review line by line in Excel, import back',
  detTbT:'Move subtitles into Excel, and back again',
  detTbL:'Export SRT / VTT to Excel or CSV, review, translate and annotate line by line in the sheet, then bring the whole table back as subtitles. Time columns stay text-exact; line breaks survive the round trip.',
  detTb1:'Time columns keep 00:00:01,000 as-is — milliseconds intact',
  detTb2:'Line breaks inside cells are restored verbatim',
  detTb3:'Chinese and English headers both work; unparseable rows are skipped',
  detTb4:'Send the sheet out for review, import it back when it returns',
  detTbCta:'Open subtitle spreadsheet tool',
  mkN14:'Milliseconds stay intact',
  tcBtN:'Batch Convert',
  tcBtD:'Convert hundreds of files into one ZIP',
  detBtT:'A whole folder of subtitles, one format change',
  detBtL:'Drag in dozens or hundreds of SRT / VTT files, convert them all to the target format and take away one ZIP. Renumbering and timestamp normalization included; unreadable files are flagged, not hidden.',
  detBt1:'Original filenames kept — only the extension changes; collisions get a suffix',
